# Local PR description drafts — never push these to the remote
.pr-description.md

# An audit store a spec wrote with no run directory to put it beside.
# `build_audit` used to fall back to an in-memory store here, which meant the
# audit ran, paid for every oracle call and dropped the records at exit; it
# writes a real file now, and a run that has a ledger still gets it beside
# that. This is the fallback landing in whatever directory the caller was in.
/audit.jsonl
